      "description": "S2 chooses an update and readout convention not specified in the passages: both next components are computed from the old weight–activity pair and current input, and only activity is read out. A readout that needs weight information must therefore have that information represented in the activity state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Doerig et al. identify stimulation as another input channel but do not specify its timing or reach. d16 makes the declared modeling choice to apply that channel after each ordinary update, including the last, as an unrestricted function on the resulting state. The passage does not claim that electrodes or TMS can realize every such function."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "d15 is exactly the claimed one-unit example: once a true input occurs, the output stays true through every later input. S2 supports the claimed inclusion rather than an equality of classes, and d16 remains an input–output function of the paired sensory and intervention inputs."
